  "strategy": "**Approach and Rationale**\n\nThe core idea behind this strategy is to reframe the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem as a constrained optimization task suitable for distributed computation. By introducing structured perturbations with the Linear Smooth Optimization method and periodically applying Entropy-based Boosted Local Searches, we target both global structure and local optima. The Discrepancy Filter Selection component helps maintain diversity in candidate solutions, mitigating the risk of premature convergence. \n\nThis approach differs from previous strategies by systematically combining gradient-based numerics optimization with adaptive compression techniques, using technique-inspired transformations and entropy-based decisions to enhance discovery in complex high-dimensional spaces.\n\n**Mathematical Specification**\n\nVariables: \n- Discretes function on grid of size n with sum constraint\n- Overlap integral defined by correlation of h with 1-h\n- Constraints: 0\u2264x\u22641 and sum(x)=n/2\n\nObjective minimization: \nMinimize C5 = max\u2096 \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx\n\n**Implementation Procedure**\n1. Initialize solution via discrepancy filtering at base resolution\n2. Apply Linear Smooth Optimization framework with dynamic weights\n3. Perform Entropy-based Boosted Local Search (EBLS) iterations\n4. Implement Discrepancy Filter Selection (DFS) for candidate diversification\n5. Use master-slave parallelism for gradient calculations\n\n**Search Choices**\n- Use adaptive smoothing parameters = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5] with budget-based selection\n- Perform 3 DFS iterations with weights 0.8, 0.6, 0.4\n- Support multi-resolution by enabling mesh-refinements\n\n**Compute Budget**\n- Time\u898b\u7a4d\u3082\u308a: LSO takes ~300s, EBLS takes ~600s\n- Use fallback solution if time projection exceeds\n- Implement early termination for non-improving trials\n\n**Validation and Return Contract**\n1. Ensure 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 and sum(h)=n/2 exactly\n2. Re-evaluate final solution in the parent's objective\n3. Set required interface/output format",
